.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/aria-hidden Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "aria-hidden"
.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
Hides from ARIA everything, except provided node(s)\&.

.PP
Helps to isolate modal dialogs and focused task - the content will be not accessible using accessible tools\&.

.PP
Now with \fRHTML inert\fP support
.SH "API"
.PP
Just call \fRhideOthers\fP with DOM-node you want to keep, and it will \fIhide\fP everything else\&. \fRtargetNode\fP could be placed anywhere - its siblings would be hidden, but it and its parents - not\&.

.PP
.RS 4
"hidden" in terms or \fRaria-hidden\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { hideOthers } from 'aria\-hidden';

const undo = hideOthers(exceptThisDOMnode);
// everything else is "aria\-hidden"

// undo changes
undo();
.fi
.PP

.PP
you also may limit the effect spread by providing top level node as a second parameter

.PP
.PP
.nf
// keep only `anotherNode` node visible in #app
// the rest of document will be untouched
hideOthers(anotherNode, document\&.getElementById('app'));
.fi
.PP

.PP
.RS 4
\fRparentNode\fP defaults to document\&.body 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Inert"
.PP
While \fRaria-hidden\fP played important role in the past and will play in the future - the main use case always was around isolating content and making elements "transparent" not only for aria, but for user interaction as well\&.

.PP
This is why you might consider using \fRinertOthers\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { hideOthers, inertOthers, supportsInert } from 'aria\-hidden';

// focus on element mean "hide others"\&. Ideally disable interactions
const focusOnElement = (node) => (supportsInert() ? inertOthers(node) : hideOthers(node));
.fi
.PP

.PP
the same function as above is already contructed and exported as

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { suppressOthers } from 'aria\-hidden';

suppressOthers([keepThisNode, andThis]);
.fi
.PP

.PP
⚠️ Note - inert \fBwill disable any interactions\fP with \fIsuppressed\fP elements ⚠️
.SS "Suppressing interactivity without inert"
One can \fRmarker\fP, the third argument to a function, to mark hidden elements\&. Later one can create a style matching given marker to apply \fRpointer-events:none\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
[hidden\-node] {
  pointer\-events: none;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
hideOthers(notThisOne, undefined /*parent = document*/, 'hidden\-node');
.fi
.PP

.PP
Generally speaking the same can be achieved by addressing \fR[aria-hidden]\fP nodes, but not all \fRaria-hidden\fP nodes are expected to be non-interactive\&. Hence, it's better to separate concerns\&.
.SH "Inspiration"
.PP
Based on \fRsmooth-ui\fP modal dialogs\&.
